.TH DIPITVHEAD 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipitvhead \- re-package transport streams as a DVB-IPI multicast, with bitrate shaping, HbbTV AIT injection, and Simulcrypt/BISS scrambling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipitvhead
.B \-i
.I uri
.RI [ per-input\ options ]
[
.B \-i
.I uri
\&...]
.RB { \-m
.IB group : port
.B |
.B \-R
.IR uri }
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
In short,
.B dipitvhead
it is a micromuxer and SCS/scrambler.
.PP
It takes one or more transport streams (multicast, http(s)+ts/hls+ts/hls+fmp4/llhls/dash/lldash, SRT, RIST or stdin)
and re-packages them as one transport stream under a new PAT/NIT with a merged EIT and rewritten PMT.
Individual SDTs can be passed, removed or overwritten.

Its output can be a DVB-IPI multicast, SRT or RIST.
It is always one transport stream, either SPTS when only one source is given, or MPTS on more.
For more output streams, run multiple instances if it.

Optionally, it scrambles selected PES using DVB SimulCrypt (multi CAS, CSA1/CSA2/CISSA, both EMMG directions) or BISS 1/2/CA (see below).
If enabled, it also adds Annex E Layer 1 FEC or CBR stuffing.

A single
.B \-i
produces a normal Single Program Transport Stream (SPTS); multiple
.B \-i
produce a Multi Program Transport Stream (MPTS), one program per input,
each connected and retried independently. One input being down never
stops output for the others. No transcoding is performed.
.PP
Input sources are given with repeatable
.B \-i
flags: multicast
.RI ( udp:// ", " rtp:// ,
RTP headers stripped automatically), HTTP/HTTPS, or stdin
.RB ( \- ).
Options marked per-input below pair with the
.B \-i
immediately preceding them, ffmpeg-style; using one before any
.B \-i
is an error. Program selection within a source is automatic (first
PAT-listed program whose PMT actually arrives) unless overridden with
.BR \-p .
.PP
Output goes to a multicast group/port
.RB ( \-m ,
RTP-wrapped by default) and/or one or more bonded RIST or SRT peers
.RB ( \-R ,
requires librist or libsrt, one scheme at a time). At least one of
.B \-m
or
.B \-R
is required. Target output bitrate can be shaped with
.BR \-b ,
combined with null-packet stuffing
.RB ( \-S )
and/or burst-limited pacing
.RB ( \-B ).
.PP
HbbTV signalling
.RB ( \-\-hbbtv )
injects an AIT (ETSI TS 102 809) advertising one AUTOSTART hybrid
broadcast/broadband application per input; this is a separate
specification from DVB-IPI itself, not a passthrough of any source AIT.
.PP
Scrambling is optional and mutually exclusive between families:
DVB SimulCrypt
.RB ( \-\-cas\-algo / \-\-cas\-ecmg\-* ,
acting as SCS and EMMG-side MUX against one or more ECMG vendors) or
BISS
.RB ( \-\-biss1\-sw / \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers ,
EBU Tech 3292): BISS1 Mode 1 (CSA1), BISS2 Mode 1/E (CISSA, static
Session Word), or BISS2 Mode CA (RSA-OAEP per-receiver entitlement).
Supported ciphers are CISSA, CSA1, and CSA2; see
.B KNOWN GAPS
below for what is not implemented.
.PP
Video: MPEG-2, H.264, HEVC. Audio: MPEG-1/2 (layers 1-3), AC-3,
E-AC-3, AAC (ADTS/LATM). Subtitles: EBU teletext, DVB bitmap.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Sources (per-input)
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIuri\fR
Input source:
.BR udp:// ,
.BR rtp:// ,
.BR http:// ,
.BR https:// ,
.BR rist://@ host:port[?query] ,
.BR srt://@ host:port ,
or
.B \-
for stdin. Repeatable.
.B rist://
takes a single peer only and requires librist;
.B @
is required, since an input peer always listens. Multiple
.B \-i rist://
entries are independent programs, not a bonded stream; use
.BR dipirist (1)
as a bridge for bonded RIST input. Each RIST input costs an extra
thread beyond what other input kinds cost.
.B srt://
takes a single peer only and requires libsrt;
.B @
is required, same reason as
.BR rist:// .
No bonding or rendezvous; use
.BR dipisrt (1)
as a bridge for that. Each SRT input costs an extra thread too.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pmt\-pid " " \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: select program by PMT PID (decimal or 0x-hex,
0x0010..0x1FFE). Default: the first live one.
.TP
.B \-\-sid \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: service_id / program_number. Default: auto-assigned,
the lowest integer not already used explicitly by another
.BR \-i .
Explicit duplicates are a startup error.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sdt " " \fItext\fR | \fB\-\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SDT service_name. Default: passthrough of the
source's own SDT.
.B \-
drops it; text sets our own.
.TP
.B \-\-provider \fItext\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SDT service_provider_name. Default: passthrough of
the source's own SDT provider, or
.B \-\-default\-provider
if
.B \-s/\-\-sdt
overrides the service_name without a
.B \-\-provider
of its own.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-provider \fIprovider\fR
SDT service_provider_name used in place of
.B dipitvhead
wherever the above
.B \-\-provider
fallback applies. Default:
.BR dipitvhead .
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: incoming multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-jitter\-ms " " \fIms\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: de-jitter buffer of 1..2000 ms for rtp://, udp://,
rist:// and srt:// inputs. RTP input is reordered by sequence number and
released after the delay. Other input is delayed in arrival order. Default: off.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-eit
For the
.B \-i
right before this: drop source EIT. Default: passed through verbatim
(SPTS) or reassembled, filtered to this program's service_id, and
merged onto the shared output EIT (MPTS).
.TP
.B \-\-strip \fIlist\fR | \fBnone\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: comma-separated list of PID classes to drop from
that source:
.B DATA
(carousels, SCTE-35, other PMT entries with an unrecognized
stream_type) and
.B ECM
(that source's own CAT/ECM/EMM passthrough). Default
.B none
(nothing dropped). Only affects what the source carried;
dipitvhead's own PAT/PMT/SDT/NIT/AIT/CAT/ECM/EMM are never touched by
this flag. Source CA/ECM passthrough is attempted only when
dipitvhead's own
.BR \-\-cas\-* /BISS
is not configured for that run.
.SS HbbTV signalling (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv \fIurl\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: inject an AIT signalling this HbbTV application's
entry-point URL. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv\-org\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: HbbTV organisation_id. Required with
.BR \-\-hbbtv .
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv\-app\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: HbbTV application_id. Required with
.BR \-\-hbbtv .
.SS RIST input (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-profile\-in \fIsimple\fR|\fImain\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this:
.B \-i rist://
only. Default:
.BR simple .
.B main
enables PSK encryption via a
.B ?secret=
query parameter on that input's URI.
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-encryption\-type\-in \fIbits\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: AES key size, 128 or 256. Requires
.BR \-\-rist\-profile\-in\ main .
.SS SRT input (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in \fIpw\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this:
.B \-i srt://
only. Enables encryption, 10..79 chars.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen\-in \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: key length. Requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in .
Default
.BR 16 .
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid\-in \fIid\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT streamid. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter\-in \fIcfg\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT packet filter config string. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency\-in \fIms\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT latency. Default: library default.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " " \fIgroup\fR:\fIport\fR
Output multicast group:port
.RI ( [ addr6 ] : port
for IPv6). Required unless
.B \-R
is given.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-out\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Outgoing multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udp
Plain UDP output. Default: RTP-wrapped. Affects
.B \-m
output only.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-ttl " " \fIn\fR
Multicast TTL / hop limit, 1..255. Default
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BR \-\-dscp " " \fIv\fR
Output DSCP marking (ETSI TS 102 034 Table 29):
.BR video-high ", " video-low ", " voice ", " signalling ", " best-effort ,
or a raw DSCP value 0..63. Default
.BR video-high .
.TP
.BR \-\-al\-fec " " \fIL\fR:\fID\fR
Annex E Layer 1 FEC (SMPTE 2022-1): sends a parity repair stream alongside
.B \-m
output.
.IR L " * " D " <= 400, " L " <= 40. Requires RTP output and "
.BR \-\-al\-fec\-port .
.TP
.BR \-\-al\-fec\-port " " \fIport\fR
Repair stream UDP port, same multicast group as
.BR \-m .
Requires
.BR \-\-al\-fec .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nit " " \fItext\fR | \fB\-\fR
NIT for the whole output.
.B \-
drops it; text sets our own. Default: SPTS passes through the
source's own NIT if present; MPTS sends no NIT.
.SS RIST output
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remote " " \fIrist://host:port\fR[\fI?query\fR]
RIST output peer, bonded with any other
.B \-R rist://
peer given, alongside
.B \-m
if given, or standalone without it. Repeatable. Mixing with
.B srt://
peers is rejected. Requires librist. Never RTP-wrapped;
.B \-u
only affects
.B \-m
output.
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-profile \fIp\fR
.B simple
or
.BR main ;
.B \-R rist://
peers only. Default
.BR simple .
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-secret \fIpsk\fR
.B \-R rist://
pre-shared key. Requires
.BR \-\-rist\-profile\ main .
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-encryption\-type \fIbits\fR
.B \-R rist://
AES key size, 128 or 256. Default: library default. Requires
.BR \-\-rist\-profile\ main .
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-cname \fIname\fR
.B \-R rist://
RTCP cname. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-buffer \fIms\fR
.B \-R rist://
recovery buffer. Default: library default.
.SS SRT output
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remote " " \fIsrt://host:port\fR
SRT output peer, bonded with any other
.B \-R srt://
peer given, alongside
.B \-m
if given, or standalone without it. Repeatable; more than one requires
.BR \-\-srt\-group\-mode .
Mixing with
.B rist://
peers is rejected. Requires libsrt. Never RTP-wrapped;
.B \-u
only affects
.B \-m
output.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-group\-mode \fIbroadcast\fR|\fIbackup\fR
Bonding mode across more than one
.B \-R srt://
peer. Required with more than one such peer, rejected with exactly one.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase \fIpw\fR
.B \-R srt://
encryption passphrase, 10..79 chars. Applies to every
.B \-R srt://
peer.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
.B \-R srt://
key length. Requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase .
Default
.BR 16 .
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid \fIid\fR
.B \-R srt://
streamid. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter \fIcfg\fR
.B \-R srt://
packet filter config string. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency \fIms\fR
.B \-R srt://
latency. Default: library default.
.SS Bitrate control
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bitrate " " \fIkbps\fR
One budget for the whole output. It counts every 188-byte packet, not the
RTP/UDP overhead. This setting alone only logs a warning when content runs
more than 2 s ahead of target. Default: no shaping, source rate passes
straight through.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-stuff
Add CBR stuffing when behind
.BR \-b 's
target, inserted ahead of the next packet and once per poll tick (<=100 ms)
while idle, at most one tick's worth each. Needs
.BR \-b .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-burst\-limit
Sleeps per datagram (7 packets) when ahead of
.BR \-b 's
target. In MPTS this stalls the shared loop, so all inputs. Needs
.BR \-b .
Combinable with
.BR \-S .
.PP
The rate holds to the packet position, but departure is datagram-granular:
output leaves in 7-packet bursts.
.SS PCR and timestamps
.TP
.BR \-\-pcr\-mode " " \fImode\fR
.BR preserve | rebase | regenerate .
Default:
.BR preserve .
.RS
.TP
.B preserve
PCR, PTS and DTS pass through untouched.
.TP
.B rebase
Source PCR plus one offset per program, the same offset on PTS and DTS.
Starts at offset 0 (output epoch = source epoch) and re-latches the offset
whenever the source PCR jumps, using the same plausibility fence as
.IR dvbipi_pcr_discontinuities_total .
Output PCR, PTS, DTS, ESCR and DTS_next_AU stay continuous across failover,
splices and reconnects.
.TP
.B regenerate
For sources whose PCR is wrong or missing. The source PCR is never copied.
PCR is computed from the output position and inserted if missing; PTS and DTS
are retimed onto the output clock. Needs
.B \-b
and
.BR \-S .
.B \-B
is recommended, without it packets can leave ahead of the PCR timeline.
.IP \(bu 2
PCR is base + (packet_index * 188 + 10) * 8 * 27 MHz / bitrate, exact integer
arithmetic, byte 10 being the one holding the last bit of the PCR base
(TR 101 290 5.3.2.1). PCR_accuracy against a CBR model is zero by construction.
.IP \(bu 2
A PCR-only packet is inserted whenever a PCR PID would go 40 ms without a PCR
(limit is 100 ms, ISO/IEC 13818-1 2.7.2). A program whose source PMT declares
no usable PCR_PID gets its video PID, else its first stream.
.IP \(bu 2
The mux clock is latched on the first PES with a PTS or DTS: first PCR = that
stamp minus the lead. The lead is
.BR \-\-pcr\-lead\-ms ,
raised to the source's own DTS-PCR distance when that is plausible (0..1 s).
1000 ms is the T-STD residency limit.
.IP \(bu 2
One time offset per program is applied to all its streams. Later programs get
the offset that puts their lead on the running clock.
.IP \(bu 2
Each stream has a hold-back queue: a packet leaves when its DTS (PTS if none)
is at most the lead ahead of the output PCR. Burst-delivering sources (HLS
segments) rely on that. A full queue (32768 packets) releases its oldest packet
early and counts it, nothing is dropped. At end of input the queues are flushed
at once.
.IP \(bu 2
The offset follows the clock difference between source and output slowly (at
most 100 ppm), from the smallest arrival lead per second of the video stream,
or the first PES stream. A backward or >2 s stamp jump, including after a
reconnect, re-latches it once.
.IP \(bu 2
Source arrival jitter shows up as lead variation at the decoder.
.B \-\-jitter\-ms
is the remedy.
.IP \(bu 2
OPCR is left alone (ISO/IEC 13818-1 2.4.3.5 forbids multiplexers to modify
it). ESCR and DTS_next_AU are shifted; the source discontinuity_indicator is
cleared, since output PCR and continuity counters are continuous. SCTE-35
pts_adjustment is shifted and CRC_32 recomputed, also for encrypted sections.
A PES header split across TS packets, or scrambled at the source, cannot be
retimed.
.IP \(bu 2
With CAS, crypto-period cadence runs off the wall clock in SPTS too, and the
scrambler is flushed after every release round, so batching never delays a
packet against its PCR position.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-pcr\-lead\-ms " " \fIms\fR
.B regenerate
only: minimum lead of DTS over PCR, 1..1000. Raised to the source's own
DTS-PCR distance when that is plausible (0..1 s). Default: 700.
.PP
On the metrics side, both
.B rebase
and
.B regenerate
export dvbipi_tv_pcr_rewritten_total, dvbipi_tv_pes_retimed_total,
dvbipi_tv_pes_retime_skipped_total, dvbipi_tv_retime_relatches_total and
dvbipi_tv_scte35_adjusted_total.
.B regenerate
adds dvbipi_tv_pcr_injected_total, dvbipi_tv_hold_forced_releases_total and
dvbipi_tv_release_lead_min_microseconds / _max_microseconds.
.SS Reliability and TLS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-error " " \fIseconds\fR
On input error, reconnect after N seconds. Default: fail once and stop
(single input only); with more than one
.B \-i
every input always retries independently regardless of this flag,
defaulting to 5 seconds when
.B \-e
is not given. Output socket and continuity counters stay up across
any gap.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Skip TLS verification (self-signed certificate, hostname, expiry).
.SS Identifiers
.TP
.B \-\-tsid \fIn\fR
transport_stream_id, 1..65535. Default
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B \-\-onid \fIn\fR
original_network_id, 1..65535. Default
.BR 1 .
.SS Logging and metrics
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
One self-updating line of stats on stderr, about once a second.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
.BR auto ", " always ", or " never .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket for metrics. Default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id. Metrics are disabled unless set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Snapshot interval in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts \fIlevel\fR
MPEG-TS health metrics level, one of
.BR off ,
.BR basic ,
.BR medium ,
.BR full .
Default
.BR off .
Requires
.BR \-\-metrics\-id .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts\-pids \fIpid,pid,...\fR
Pids that carry data the PMT does not reference (for example private streams) and that the
.B full
level of
.B \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts
should treat as known. Packets on them still count in
.BR dvbipi_ts_unreferenced_packets_total ,
and their first appearance is left out of
.BR dvbipi_ts_unreferenced_unlisted_pids_total .
Setting this option also gives every pid the PMT references (at most 32 per stream) its own packet and scrambled packet counters,
.B dvbipi_ts_pid_packets_total
and
.BR dvbipi_ts_pid_scrambled_packets_total ,
labeled
.BR pid ,
and the same counted per service over all pids its PMT references,
.B dvbipi_ts_service_packets_total
and
.BR dvbipi_ts_service_scrambled_packets_total ,
labeled
.BR service .
Decimal or 0x hex, 0 to 8191. Requires
.BR \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts\ full .
.SS Conditional access: Simulcrypt
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-algo \fIa\fR
Enable CAS:
.BR cissa ", " csa2 ", or " csa1 .
Default: disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg \fIep\fR
ECMG address,
.BR tcp://host:port .
Repeatable, one CAS vendor per
.BR \-\-cas\-ecmg .
Required with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: protocol version
.BR 2 " or " 3 .
Default: auto-negotiate.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-super\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: Super_CAS_id, decimal or 0x-hex. Required per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: ECM_id. Required per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: output PID for its ECM stream. Default
.BR 0x0020 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-port \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: our EMMG listener port. Default
.BR 8002 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-max\-conns \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: max concurrent EMMG client connections, 1..64.
Default
.BR 8 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: EMMG protocol version
.BR 2 " or " 3 .
Default: accept the client's proposal.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-reverse \fItcp://host:port\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: dial out to this EMMG instead of listening for it.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cas\-emmg\-port " and " \-\-cas\-emmg\-max\-conns .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: output PID for its EMM stream. Default
.BR 0x0021 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-resilience \fIr\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: behavior on its own ECMG loss:
.BR frozen ", " cycling ", or " silent .
Default
.BR frozen .
.B frozen
keeps scrambling with the last known-good control word until the
ECMG returns.
.B cycling
keeps flipping parity on schedule between the last two known control
words instead of freezing on one.
.B silent
stops resending that vendor's ECM stream while its ECMG is
unreachable; content stays scrambled with the last known-good control
word, same as
.BR frozen .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-required
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: its outage forces the global fallback (see
.B \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear
below) regardless of other vendors.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-algo \fIa\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: encrypt
.BR CW_provision 's
control word per ETSI TS 103 197 Annex D. As specified,
.B des56
is supported. However, it allows extensions, so we used it as
generic as possible for some modern interpretation.
.BR des56 ", " aes128 ", or " aes256 .
Default: off (plaintext, today's behavior).
.B des56
is the spec-literal single-DES scheme. Included for interop, not as
a recommendation.
.BR aes128 " and " aes256
are a generic extension of the same Annex D parameter framing.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-aes\-mode \fIm\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this:
.BR stream " or " ecb ,
.BR aes128 / aes256
only. Default
.BR stream .
.B ecb
is rejected when this vendor's control word is 8 bytes (AES has no
8-byte block mode).
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-fixed\-key \fIhex\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: fixed key, hex-encoded:
14 chars for
.BR des56 ,
32 for
.BR aes128 ,
64 for
.BR aes256 .
Default: for
.BR des56 ,
Annex D's own published ROM key; no default for
.BR aes128 / aes256 ,
which fail at startup instead if a key list is not configured either.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-a \fIpath\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: Annex D key list file, exactly 2048 raw bytes.
Either this or
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-fixed\-key
selects the key addressing mode used per
.BR CW_provision .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-b \fIpath\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: second Annex D key list file, same format as
.BR \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-a .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-pids \fIlist\fR
PIDs to scramble: comma-separated output-side PIDs (decimal or
0x-hex) and/or the
.BR video / audio / lcevc
keywords, meaning every video/audio/LCEVC elementary stream on the
output. Freely mixable, e.g.
.BR 0x0103,video .
Default
.B video,audio
(all video and audio streams) -
.B lcevc
is never implied by either, or by the default: scrambling an LCEVC
enhancement stream is always an explicit choice. Content is scrambled
exactly once regardless of vendor count; also used, with the same
default, under any BISS mode below.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cp\-duration \fIms\fR
Crypto-period duration in milliseconds, 1..86400000, shared by every
vendor. Default
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear
On total outage (every vendor down, or a
.B \-\-cas\-required
vendor down specifically): go clear-to-air instead of staying
scrambled on the last known-good control word.
.SS Conditional access: BISS
.TP
.B \-\-biss1\-sw \fIhex12\fR
Enable legacy BISS1 Mode 1: 12 hex char Session Word, scrambles with
CSA1. BISS1 Mode E (DES) is not supported. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-sw \fIhex32\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode 1/E: 32 hex char Session Word, scrambles with CISSA.
No ECMG/EMMG. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-emit\-esw \fIid\fR
With
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw :
log the AES-128-ECB Encrypted Session Word for this 32 hex char receiver
ID, for out-of-band distribution.
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers \fIdir\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode CA (EBU Tech 3292-s1): directory of PKCS#8 PEM
public key files (any number of keys each), one key per entitled receiver
or group of receivers sharing a key pair. Entries over 15 are split across
EMM sections. Rescan by
.BR SIGHUP .
A receiver removed from the directory is revoked, forcing an
immediate Session Key change. Requires
.B \-\-cas\-cp\-duration
of at least 1000 (T_ECM_change_min). The Session Key rotates every
6th Session Word period. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-biss1\-sw / \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-session\-id \fIn\fR
Administratively unique entitlement_session_id, decimal or 0x-hex,
16-bit. Default: random at startup.
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\ \fI<path>\fR
YAML configuration file. Keys mirror the options above. Without this option,
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipitvhead.yaml
is read if it exists.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-strict
Treat configuration file issues (unknown or duplicate keys, invalid values,
conflicting settings, unreadable referenced files) as errors instead of
warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-configtest
Check the configuration file (from
.B \-c
or the default location) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH PID ALLOCATION
Mux-wide, fixed, shared by every program (DVB-SI reserved range,
ETSI EN 300 468): PAT
.BR 0x0000 ,
NIT
.BR 0x0010 ,
SDT
.BR 0x0011 ,
EIT
.BR 0x0012 ,
CAT
.BR 0x0001 .
.PP
Every other table is per-program, in a fixed 32-PID block keyed to
that input's 0-based position (i) among the
.B \-i
flags: PMT 0x1000+i, video 0x0100+i*32, other elementary streams
0x0101+i*32 upward in discovery order, AIT 0x011F+i*32. A single
.B \-i
is i=0, identical to before per-program blocks existed.
.SH MULTIPLE INPUTS (MPTS)
More than one
.B \-i
produces an MPTS. Servicing is one poll loop, not one thread per
input, taken in round-robin order so no input is always serviced
last; each input is capped at 32 TS packets read per tick so one busy
source can't starve the others that tick. De-jitter buffering is off
unless
.B \-\-jitter\-ms
is given for an input.
.PP
With
.B \-\-pcr\-mode preserve
(default) each program keeps forwarding its own source's PCR untouched.
There is no synthesized mux-wide clock, so a program's timing stays
accurate to its own source regardless of what the others are doing.
.B rebase
keeps that per-program timing and shifts it by a per-program offset.
.B regenerate
puts every program on one shared mux clock.
.PP
The per-program elementary-stream cap is 31 real streams, one slot
always reserved for AIT whether
.B \-\-hbbtv
is used on that input or not. Extras beyond that are dropped in
discovery order, logged once per program setup.
.PP
It is one process, one thread doing the demux/remux/CAS work for
every program on a running instance. Capacity is a CPU budget
question, not a thread or connection limit; plan program count per
instance, and instance count per host, with that in mind.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
CAS support is a build-time option
.RI ( DIPITVHEAD_CAS ,
on by default). CISSA needs OpenSSL. CSA1, CSA2, and BISS1 dlopen
.I libdvbcsa
at runtime if present; dipitvhead is not built against it and does
not bundle it, and static release tarballs do not contain it either.
RIST input/output needs
.IR librist ,
SRT input/output needs
.IR libsrt ,
same as every other tool in this toolkit. HTTPS input is a
build-time option too
.RI ( \-DDVBIPITOOLS_TLS=OFF ,
auto-off without OpenSSL). Missing any of these degrades that
feature to unavailable, not a build failure.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the BISS2 Mode CA receivers directory
.RB ( \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers )
and apply any added, removed, or changed keys.
.SH KNOWN LIMITATIONS
* CISSA, CSA1, CSA2, BISS1 Mode 1, BISS2 Mode 1/E, and BISS2 Mode CA
only.

* No CSA3, no BISS1 Mode E (DES). BISS2 Mode CA: at most 3840
receiver or group keys.

* No entitlement_priv_data_loop vendor extensions:
prevent_descrambled_forward/prevent_decoded_forward/insert_watermark
entitlement flags are always 0 (unenforced).

* It is a single-pass scrambler, there is no re-scrambling of already-scrambled input.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-s "My Channel"
Basic SPTS: one RTP source re-streamed with its own SDT service name.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i udp://@239.0.0.1:5000 \-m 239.5.5.5:6000 \-b 3000 \-S \-B \-\-pcr\-mode regenerate
Source with wrong or missing PCR: rebuild PCR and timestamps on a 3 Mbit/s CBR timeline.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i https://host/live/x/y.ts \-k \-m 239.1.1.2:5000 \-b 8000 \-S \-B
HTTPS source with a self-signed certificate, bitrate-shaped to
8000 kbps with stuffing and burst limiting.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-\-sdt "Channel A" \-i rtp://@239.19.75.2:8700 \-\-sdt "Channel B" \-m 239.1.1.3:5000 \-e 5
MPTS: two RTP sources merged into one output, each its own program,
5-second reconnect on input error.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i udp://@239.0.0.1:5000 \-m 239.5.5.5:6000 \-\-hbbtv https://example.org/hbbtv/ \-\-hbbtv\-org\-id 1 \-\-hbbtv\-app\-id 100
Inject an HbbTV AUTOSTART application AIT alongside the program.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-cas\-algo cissa \-\-cas\-ecmg tcp://ecmg.example:2222 \-\-cas\-super\-id 0x4A750002 \-\-cas\-ecm\-id 1
Scramble an SPTS via Simulcrypt CISSA against one ECMG vendor.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss2\-sw 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff
BISS2 Mode 1/E: static 32 hex char Session Word, no ECMG/EMMG needed.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss1\-sw 0123456789ab
Legacy BISS1 Mode 1: 12 hex char Session Word, CSA1.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers /etc/biss\-ca/receivers
BISS2 Mode CA: per-receiver RSA entitlement, one PEM pubkey per file
under the directory.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-R rist://recv1.example:2000 \-R rist://recv2.example:2000 \-\-rist\-profile main \-\-rist\-secret s3cr3t12345
RIST output bonded to two peers, PSK-encrypted.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-R srt://recv.example:9000 \-\-srt\-passphrase s3cr3t12345
SRT output to a single peer, encrypted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipitvhead.yaml
Default configuration file, read if present. A commented template with all
defaults ships as
.IR /usr/share/dvbipitools/etc/dipitvhead.yaml .
